To support RISC-V hardware recommendations, I will update the application to specifically prioritize lightweight, GGUF-based models when "RISC-V" is selected as the CPU type.

1.  **`data/localModels.ts`**: I will add and refine specific "Edge/RISC-V" optimized models (like Qwen 0.5B/1.5B and TinyLlama) and explicitly tag them with `RISC-V` in their hardware requirements.
2.  **`services/localReasoning.ts`**: I will add specific scoring logic to `calculateFitScore`. If the user selects RISC-V, the engine will heavily penalize large models, boost GGUF models (since CUDA/Metal won't work), and prioritize models tagged for "Edge" or "RISC-V".

